    "key": "w2a-tips-luul-winter",
    "authorHandle": "luul_dukaan",
    "type": "update",
    "title": "Winterising a Lake Street shop entrance — what actually works",
    "body": "Minnesota winter is coming for your doorway, new shopkeepers. After many winters on Lake Street: 1) Heavy-duty entry mats, two of them — one outside, one inside — replaced before they become ice sculptures. 2) A cheap plastic vestibule does more for your heating bill than any thermostat argument with your staff. 3) Pet-safe ice melt only; regular salt eats the floor and customers track it everywhere. 4) Keep the shovel INSIDE the shop — the outside one walks away every single year. My mother learned all this starting with one shelf in 1998. You get it for free.",
    "tags": [
      "community",
      "e-commerce"
    ],
    "daysAgo": 11,
