    "title": "How verification calls actually work (and how to book)",
    "body": "Demystifying the blue tick, since I get the same five questions weekly. What it is: a ten-minute video call with me where we confirm you are who your profile says — ID for identity verification, a business document for business verification. What it is not: an interview, a test of your English, or a background check. What to have ready: your document, decent light, and your own face. Privacy: calls are recorded to an access-logged vault; moderators cannot watch them, and I cannot see your reports — different doors, different keys. Nervous? Most people are, for about ninety seconds. Booking: my profile, then Book a slot. Evenings fill first; mornings are quiet.",
