    "body": "Milestone from the verification desk: the first 10 verification calls are complete. Since this process should never be a mystery, here is how it actually goes: a booked slot, a five-minute video chat, I confirm you are the person in your profile, and that is it. Recordings are access-logged and never shared with moderators — verifier and mod are separate jobs by design, and I intend to keep it that way. What surprised me, honestly: (1) How nervous people are when they join — and how fast that disappears once they realise it is a conversation, not an interrogation. Everyone so far has arrived early. Early! (2) Nobody treats the badge as decoration. Every single person had a practical reason — a trade partner who asked for it, a listing they want trusted, a DM they want answered. Verification here is commerce infrastructure, not vanity. (3) My favourite call: an elder who brought his grandson to translate, and by minute three was telling me the history of his market stall while the grandson begged him to answer the actual questions. Verified, obviously. Ten down. If you have booked a slot: see you there, arrive as nervous as you like. If you are wondering whether to book: the queue is open and the water is warm.",
