    "body": "I have spent years, here and elsewhere, saying that community savings groups are unauditable — warm feelings wrapped around unverifiable numbers, waiting for the day the treasurer's cousin needs a loan. I said versions of this on this platform, with citations, and I would say most of it again. But dood wadaag cuts both ways, and a sceptic who never updates is just a cynic with a bibliography. So, publicly: after cycle 12 closed, I asked Iskaashato Hooyo whether an outsider could examine their ledger. They said yes — the same open books their members see. I checked twelve cycles of records against the payout schedule. It reconciles. Every cycle, every member, a volunteer audit committee, and a paper trail my old economics department would accept without blushing. My general prior stands: most schemes that want your money still deserve every uncomfortable question I can generate, and the difference here is not good intentions — it is auditability. But this specific co-op has earned the thing I ration most carefully: trust. I demand public updates from everyone else when the evidence moves. Consider this mine.",
