    "type": "ask",
    "title": "Hiring my first real employee in Kenya — contract gotchas?",
    "body": "Business milestone with homework attached. My head baker has been with me a year on an informal arrangement — she is the reason the halwa sells out by noon, and I want to do this properly: a real contract, a real payslip, everything official. It is my first time being An Employer and I am equal parts proud and terrified. Questions for anyone who has hired in Kenya: (1) What must be in a written contract, and what do people always forget? (2) How does probation work — how long, and what happens at the end? (3) What do I need to register for as an employer — taxes, statutory contributions — and in what order? (4) The gotcha question: what is the mistake first-time employers make that nobody warns you about? The next batch of kac kac is dedicated to whoever saves me from a fine.",
    "tags": [
      "jobs",
      "food"
    ],
    "daysAgo": 7,
