        "body": "Adding the tax side, with the caveat that I practise in the Netherlands — treat this as a checklist for your local accountant, not gospel. Register as an employer with the revenue authority before her first official payday; PAYE comes out of her salary and is remitted monthly, and the statutory contributions (social security and the health fund) carry employer portions too — budget those on top of her gross, not inside it. Keep every payslip and remittance receipt from day one: clean payroll records are cheap to keep and expensive to reconstruct. And Fartuun is right about the service-date question — ask about that one specifically. My pro-bono Saturday is the first of the month if you want a second pair of eyes on the setup.",
